## Important finding up front

The `planProgress` view is **already fully implemented** in `AutomationAPI`. The class already declares `VIEW_PLAN_PROGRESS = "planProgress"`, registers it in the constructor, handles it in `handleApiView`, and builds the response via a `progressResponse(AutomationPlan)` helper. There is no separate/new view to add — the pattern you'd follow for a "planProgress" view is the pattern this file already uses. (There is also no existing unit test referencing it — see item 6.)

---

## 1. File defining `AutomationAPI`

`/workspace/repo/addOns/automation/src/main/java/org/zaproxy/addon/automation/AutomationAPI.java`

Package `org.zaproxy.addon.automation`, `public class AutomationAPI extends ApiImplementor`.

## 2. `handleApiView` + surrounding class context

The class registers one action set and the view in its constructor:

```java
private static final String VIEW_PLAN_PROGRESS = "planProgress";
private static final String PARAM_PLAN_ID = "planId";
private static final String ELEMENT_INFO = "info";
private static final String ELEMENT_WARN = "warn";
private static final String ELEMENT_ERROR = "error";
...
public AutomationAPI(ExtensionAutomation extension) {
    super();
    this.extension = extension;
    this.addApiAction(new ApiAction(ACTION_RUN_PLAN, new String[] {PARAM_FILE_PATH}));
    this.addApiAction(new ApiAction(ACTION_END_DELAY_JOB));
    this.addApiView(new ApiView(VIEW_PLAN_PROGRESS, new String[] {PARAM_PLAN_ID}));
}
```

`handleApiView` (lines 105-119) and its helper `progressResponse` (lines 121-151):

```java
@Override
public ApiResponse handleApiView(String name, JSONObject params) throws ApiException {
    LOGGER.debug("handleApiView {} {}", name, params);

    if (name.equals(VIEW_PLAN_PROGRESS)) {
        AutomationPlan plan = extension.getPlan(params.getInt(PARAM_PLAN_ID));

        if (plan == null) {
            throw new ApiException(Type.DOES_NOT_EXIST);
        }

        return progressResponse(plan);
    }
    throw new ApiException(Type.BAD_VIEW);
}

ApiResponse progressResponse(AutomationPlan plan) {
    HashMap<String, Object> map = new HashMap<>();
    map.put(PARAM_PLAN_ID, plan.getId());

    if (plan.getStarted() != null) {
        map.put("started", plan.getStarted());
    }
    if (plan.getFinished() != null) {
        map.put("finished", plan.getFinished());
    }

    ApiResponseList infoMsgs = new ApiResponseList(ELEMENT_INFO);
    plan.getProgress().getInfos().stream()
            .map(msg -> new ApiResponseElement(ELEMENT_INFO, msg))
            .forEach(infoMsgs::addItem);
    map.put(ELEMENT_INFO, infoMsgs);

    ApiResponseList warnMsgs = new ApiResponseList(ELEMENT_WARN);
    plan.getProgress().getWarnings().stream()
            .map(msg -> new ApiResponseElement(ELEMENT_WARN, msg))
            .forEach(warnMsgs::addItem);
    map.put(ELEMENT_WARN, warnMsgs);

    ApiResponseList errorMsgs = new ApiResponseList(ELEMENT_ERROR);
    plan.getProgress().getErrors().stream()
            .map(msg -> new ApiResponseElement(ELEMENT_ERROR, msg))
            .forEach(errorMsgs::addItem);
    map.put(ELEMENT_ERROR, errorMsgs);

    return new ApiResponseSet<>(VIEW_PLAN_PROGRESS, map);
}
```

`handleApiAction` (lines 78-103) handles `runPlan` (loads/registers/runs a plan, returns `planId`) and `endDelayJob`.

## 3. `ApiResponse` class/type (path + serialization)

These are **ZAP core** types, not in this repo. They come from the dependency `org.zaproxy:zap:2.14.0` (jar at `/root/.gradle/caches/modules-2/files-2.1/org.zaproxy/zap/2.14.0/.../zap-2.14.0.jar`), package `org.zaproxy.zap.extension.api`. Source: `github.com/zaproxy/zaproxy` tag `v2.14.0`, `zap/src/main/java/org/zaproxy/zap/extension/api/`.

**`ApiResponse` (abstract base):**
```java
public abstract class ApiResponse {
    private String name;
    public ApiResponse(String name) { this.name = name; }
    public String getName() { return name; }
    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }
    public abstract JSON toJSON();
    public abstract void toXML(Document doc, Element rootElement);
    public abstract void toHTML(StringBuilder sb);
    public abstract String toString(int indent);
}
```

**`ApiResponseElement extends ApiResponse`** — a name + string value (or a nested `ApiResponse`). Has static `OK`/`FAIL`. Constructors include `ApiResponseElement(String name, String value)` (the one used in `progressResponse`).
```java
public JSON toJSON() {
    JSONObject jo = new JSONObject();
    if (apiResponse == null) {
        jo.put(getName(), value == null ? JSONNull.getInstance()
                                        : JsonUtil.getJsonFriendlyString(value));
    } else {
        jo.put(getName(), apiResponse.toJSON().toString());
    }
    return jo;
}
public void toXML(Document doc, Element parent) {
    if (apiResponse == null) {
        parent.appendChild(doc.createTextNode(
            getValue() != null ? XMLStringUtil.escapeControlChrs(getValue()) : ""));
    } else {
        apiResponse.toXML(doc, parent);
    }
}
```
Note: for XML the element name is NOT written here — the parent element (created by the caller/`ApiResponseList`) carries the name.

**`ApiResponseList extends ApiResponse`** — holds `List<ApiResponse>`; `addItem(ApiResponse)` appends.
```java
public JSON toJSON() {
    if (list == null) return null;
    JSONObject jo = new JSONObject();
    JSONArray array = new JSONArray();
    jo.put(getName(), array);                 // e.g. {"info":[...]}
    for (ApiResponse resp : list) {
        if (resp instanceof ApiResponseElement) {
            jo.getJSONArray(getName()).add(
                JsonUtil.getJsonFriendlyString(((ApiResponseElement) resp).getValue()));
        } else {
            jo.getJSONArray(getName()).add(resp.toJSON().toString());
        }
    }
    return jo;
}
public void toXML(Document doc, Element parent) {
    parent.setAttribute("type", "list");
    for (ApiResponse resp : list) {
        Element el = doc.createElement(resp.getName());
        resp.toXML(doc, el);
        parent.appendChild(el);
    }
}
```
So a list of `ApiResponseElement("info", msg)` serializes to JSON as an array of the string values under key `"info"`.

**`ApiResponseSet<T> extends ApiResponse`** — wraps `Map<String,T>`. This is the top-level object returned by `progressResponse`.
```java
public ApiResponseSet(String name, Map<String, T> values) { super(name); this.values = values; }
public JSON toJSON() {
    if (values == null) return null;
    JSONObject jo = new JSONObject();
    for (Entry<String, T> val : values.entrySet()) {
        T value = val.getValue();
        if (value instanceof String) {
            jo.put(val.getKey(), JsonUtil.getJsonFriendlyString((String) value));
        } else {
            jo.put(val.getKey(), value);      // ApiResponseList values recurse here
        }
    }
    return jo;
}
public void toXML(Document doc, Element parent) {
    parent.setAttribute("type", "set");
    for (Entry<String, T> val : values.entrySet()) {
        Element el = doc.createElement(val.getKey());
        String textValue = val.getValue() == null ? "" : val.getValue().toString();
        el.appendChild(doc.createTextNode(XMLStringUtil.escapeControlChrs(textValue)));
        parent.appendChild(el);
    }
}
```
Net JSON shape of the planProgress response: `{ "planId": <int>, "started": ..., "finished": ..., "info": ["..."], "warn": ["..."], "error": ["..."] }` (started/finished present only when non-null).

